Keep bounded fallback polling active for every registered interest. Solaris
event-port delivery is one-shot and an edge can be lost after a descriptor is
re-associated. Removing a drained direction from fallback therefore restores
the permanent port_getn wait this fallback is intended to prevent.

The event port remains the low-latency path. The ten millisecond poll is a
reliability backstop and supplies level-like readiness to Tokio.

